{
  "dom_id": "step-e5558",
  "name": "Example: Calculating a Minimum Value Using the Triangle Inequality",
  "problem": "Given that $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} +3\\mathbf{v} \\Vert=14$ and $\\Vert \\mathbf{v} \\Vert=2,$ find the smallest possible value of $\\Vert \\mathbf{u}\\Vert.$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016u+3v\u2016 & \\le \u2016u\u2016+\u20163v\u2016.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016u+3v\u2016 & \\le \u2016u\u2016+3\u2016v\u2016 \\\\ 14 & \\le \u2016u\u2016+3(2) \\\\ 14 & \\le \u2016u\u2016+6 \\\\ 8 & \\le \u2016u\u2016.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert$ is $8.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
